; NextDAAD 256-colour text fixture.
;
; Compiled by tests\build-tests.ps1 on every run and asserted at the
; byte level there; staged as the active GAME.DDB in sd\PALETTE\ by
; tests\build-tests.ps1 -Palette.
;
; WHAT IT PINS
; DRC declares INK, PAPER and BORDER as a single generic value
; parameter checked only against 0-255, so a value above 15 is
; expressible in the database today. This fixture authors such values
; and the harness asserts the exact bytes reached the DDB, so a future
; toolchain change that starts folding them is caught immediately.
;
; LOOK prints one line in each of four extended combinations, then a
; 16-colour block that must still render exactly as it did before the
; 256-colour work. EXAMINE walks 32 ink values against one paper, which
; is the pair allocator's pressure test.

/CTL
_
/VOC
LOOK   4  verb
EXAMINE 5 verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key."
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "INK 200 on PAPER 37#n"
/1 "INK 224 on PAPER 0#n"
/2 "INK 28 on PAPER 224#n"
/3 "INK 255 on PAPER 3#n"
/4 "classic ink 7 paper 0#n"
/5 "classic ink 15 paper 1#n"
/6 "classic ink 0 paper 6#n"
/7 "pressure block#n"
/8 "X"
/OTX
/0 "a thing"
/LTX
/0 "Colour arena."
/CON
/0
/OBJ
/0    0   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
> _ _        CLS
             BORDER 224
             PAPER 37
             INK 200
             MESSAGE 0
             PAPER 0
             INK 224
             MESSAGE 1
             PAPER 224
             INK 28
             MESSAGE 2
             PAPER 3
             INK 255
             MESSAGE 3
             PAPER 0
             INK 7
             MESSAGE 4
             PAPER 1
             INK 15
             MESSAGE 5
             PAPER 6
             INK 0
             MESSAGE 6
             PROCESS 1
/PRO 1
> LOOK _     DESC 0
             DONE
> EXAMINE _  PAPER 0
             INK 7
             MESSAGE 7
             PAPER 64
             INK 16
             MESSAGE 8
             INK 17
             MESSAGE 8
             INK 18
             MESSAGE 8
             INK 19
             MESSAGE 8
             INK 20
             MESSAGE 8
             INK 21
             MESSAGE 8
             INK 22
             MESSAGE 8
             INK 23
             MESSAGE 8
             DONE
/END
